    "title": "Arduino Nano (SKU A000005): Full Pinout PDF, Schematic NanoV3.3 (headers J1 and J2), and User Manual",
    "url": "https://docs.arduino.cc/resources/pinouts/A000005-full-pinout.pdf",
    "url2": "https://docs.arduino.cc/resources/schematics/A000005-schematics.pdf",
    "url3": "https://docs.arduino.cc/resources/datasheets/A000005-datasheet.pdf",
    "revision": "Nano V3.3 (A000005); full pinout 'Last update: 30/06/2021'; schematic 'NanoV3.3 23/01/19'; datasheet Rev 5 'Modified: 19/11/2026'",
    "retrieved": "2026-11-26",
    "pinNumbering": "Pins 1-30 follow the standard DIP-30 pinout of the two 15-pin headers on the schematic: pins 1-15 are J1-1 to J1-15 (D1/TX through D12/MISO) and pins 16-30 are J2-15 down to J2-1 (D13/SCK through VIN), matching the datasheet Features section (pin 27 is +5V, pin 30 is VIN).",
    "notes": "GND pins 4 and 29 form group GND; RESET pins 3 and 28 form group RESET. A0-A5 also function as digital pins D14-D19 (aliases); A6 and A7 are analog-only inputs on the ATmega328P TQFP-32. I2C uses A4 (SDA) and A5 (SCL). SPI uses D10 (SS), D11 (COPI/MOSI), D12 (CIPO/MISO) and D13 (SCK/LED_BUILTIN). Roles: +5V and +3V3 are power_out (on-board regulator outputs), VIN is power_in (7-12 V)."
  },
